bsolete) A young goat; a kid.", "tags": ["countable", "obsolete", "uncountable"], "examples": ["The Holy Bible, […] (King James Version), London: […] Robert Barker, […], 1611, →OCLC, Exodus 12:5: “Your lamb shall be without blemish, a male of the first year: ye shall take it out from the sheep, or from the goats:”"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(uncountable) The flesh of a lamb used as food; (sometimes loosely) the flesh of a sheep of any age used as food.", "tags": ["uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(figuratively) A person who is meek, docile, and easily led.", "tags": ["countable", "figuratively", "uncountable"], "examples": ["Near-synonym: sheep"], "quotes": [], "synonyms": ["sheep"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Lambskin.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "They were as alike as prisoners, dressed in black silk waists and fitted skirts, with shawls of crimped black lamb across their shoulders.", "reference": "1934, Kay Boyle, My Next Bride, Virago, published 1986, page 8:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "A simple, unsophisticated person.", "tags": ["countable", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(finance, slang) One who ignorantly speculates on the stock exchange and is victimized.", "tags": ["countable", "slang", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(slang) A fan of American singer, songwriter, actress, and record producer Mariah Carey (born 1969).", "tags": ["countable", "slang", "uncountable"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "Part of me revels in the campiness of